WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.075
Module ten:

2
00:00:01.075 --> 00:00:02.591
risk and position size.

3
00:00:02.591 --> 00:00:08.061
Why drawdown is more dangerous than it looks, how to size a position from the stop,

4
00:00:08.061 --> 00:00:12.542
what the Kelly criterion is, and why constant leverage eats capital.

5
00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:17.938
Drawdown is how far capital is below its previous peak.

6
00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:20.496
Its main nastiness is asymmetry.

7
00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:23.773
After minus 50 percent you need plus 100.

8
00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:28.968
After minus 83, bitcoin's worst fall, a rise of almost six times.

9
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.206
After minus 96, of 25 times.

10
00:00:32.206 --> 00:00:34.744
Not only depth matters but also duration:

11
00:00:34.744 --> 00:00:38.521
how many days in a row capital stays below its previous peak.

12
00:00:38.521 --> 00:00:43.102
That is the time you will have to sit through without abandoning the idea.
